;; Problem statements, one per stage of the run, written before the stage is built (docs/RICH-HICKEY.md,
;; "And the hammock."): the problem, the information it needs that the bot does not yet gather, what
;; can go wrong, what done means in world terms, and what the last recorded failure showed. Hand-written
;; data next to goals.edn; problems_test requires a statement for every target goal and checks every
;; source exists. Stages already built cite our own recorded failures; stages ahead cite the siblings
;; (steve, ruststeve), whose notes in brain/siblings are research drafts until re-verified.
;; Update a row when a run of that stage fails in a new way: the failure is the most valuable line here.
[{:problem/stage :wood
  :problem/goals [:wood]
  :problem/statement
  "Hold one log from a natural tree, starting wherever the bot lands, with only what the server has sent it."
  :problem/needs
  ["Which loaded blocks are logs, and which log of a trunk is at feet height."
   "Where its own drop is, and whether a leaf covers it."
   "Whether the landing itself is usable: not water, not inside a canopy, not buried."]
  :problem/risks
  ["A drop lands under the trunk, out of a 1.8-tall player's reach."
   "A branch passes for a trunk bottom, or the trunk stands on a bank above the bot: the drop rests out of the pickup box."
   "A leaf at head height hides the drop and walking cannot pass it."
   "The fixture lands the bot on a pond, in a canopy or in stone."
   "An early FINISH aborts the break."]
  :problem/done "The server's inventory read for the bot shows any *_log."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Recorded in CI and replayed: collect failed :not-picked-up when the bot dug the base log from two blocks above (fixed by trunk-target), and again when a low oak leaf covered the drop (fixed by digging the blocker). Recorded live 2026-10-10 on a pickaxe run and diagnosed by folding the recording: three collects in a row failed :not-picked-up because the drop lay one block up a ledge with leaves one above head height over the ledge and over the bot, so no jump rose a full block (fixed: over a one-block step, the blocker also looks one above the head, in both columns). Recorded by the gym (batch wood-a2 run 5) and again by a plan (smoke2 run 5), landing 21280,18720, and diagnosed by folding the recording: the bot took a branch log (air under it) for a trunk bottom and its drop came to rest on the trunk below; then, standing in a pit, it dug the real base on a bank four blocks above its feet and that drop rested above its pickup box; each failed walk blacklisted one log, not the tree, so it kept choosing the same trunk until the plan failed :stuck. Fixed: a trunk bottom stands on ground (or over its own dug base), a log walk arrives only with the drop's resting height within pickup reach of the feet, and a failed log intent blacklists its whole trunk (sim scenarios a-drop-out-of-reach-is-never-dug-for and a-trunk-on-a-bank-is-taken-from-the-bank). The forest property now generates branches and banks 1-2 high; a tree on a 2-high bank holds its drop beyond a pickup from the ground, and the bot gives it up (:no-log when it is the only tree). Race 38674091115 (issue #87) climbed it instead: out is not at the trees, and a trunk remembered above the eye no walk reaches is now climbed toward (wood/trees-climb), the forest property now accepts a 2-high bank when the climb succeeds (world {:x 13, :z 3, :h 3, :mound 2} seed 386881739251), while retaining :no-log for unsupported banks. The walk now follows a planned route (issue #4): a pond or a two-block ledge between the bot and the trunk, which ended :stuck and blacklisted the trunk, is routed around or climbed by its step (sim scenario a-log-across-a-cliff-and-a-pond-is-reached-by-a-route). Race 38477665442 (issue #38, 39 bots, and the sim race in the same worlds): every bot landed on snowy ground never moved, twelve walks failing :no-path in a second, because one layer of snow lay on every block round it and a route took that layer for an awkward shape, so neither the feet cell nor any beside it could be stood on and every plan was :none from nowhere. Fixed: one layer of snow has no collision shape in the game and the physics passes through it, so a route does too (path/one-layer-snow; path-test a-snowfield-is-crossed-through-its-one-layer-snow). Race 38477665442 (2026-10-13, issue #57, 20 real runs): bots Clj_r14 and Clj_r20 and their runners' twins landed on a lake's shore with every remembered trunk across the water; each walk at one failed :no-path, and once every trunk in reach was given up the gather waited :no-log until the plan failed, the forest beyond the hill never loaded. Under the open sky with no route to any trunk the gather now hunts toward the nearest log, as a water hunt goes out, forty blocks at a time (wood/hunt). Race 38665691517 (issue #57): landings with no standing trunk in reach waited :no-log at the landing round after round, routes out on three bearings; the wood hunt now sets out with no log known (wood/hunt). Race 38680745815 runner 5 (issue #57, 2026-10-15): under server load the planner now counts waits in ticks, and a hunt with remembered trees can walk toward them after leaving the landing. Sim race 38811417241 runner 2 (issue #87, world R2/20): out of the mine on a block in a powder-snow field, powder snow neither floor nor clear to a route left no move toward a spruce eight blocks off and the plan waited :no-log at the ingots; powder snow is passable now (no collision for a player), routes go through it, and climb-out asks only the nearest logs whether they are standing trunks. Same round (world R3/4): on a sand island at its landing with every trunk a hundred blocks across a lake and every hunt bearing at water, the plan waited :no-log; it now swims across toward the nearest remembered trunk (wood/crossing, swim :cross). Sim race 38844589684 runner 6 (issue #57, world R1/30 seed 4): on a sand headland with the trees across a lake, the crossing swam forty blocks and stuck eight short against a far bank too high to climb, failing :stuck three times; a crossing stuck in the water now swims for the nearest bank and ends there. Real race (issue #57, Clj_r07): out on a mountain top at y 238 with the nearest trunk 56 below and 60 across, no route to it, the plan waited :no-log; it now cuts stairs down toward it (wood/trees-descend). Sim world R1/4 (issues #370, #186) and real-2/1 (issue #87): a small tree three to twelve blocks off and a few under the feet, walled in by its own leaves, no route, the walk's failure giving its grove up: a level run through the leaves to beside the trunk (wood/trees-tunnel), the log that falls under the leaves the bot stands on collected by digging that leaf and centring over the drop (intent/leaf-under). Sim race 39934917165 (issue #89, world R1/23) and real-6 s1 Clj_r07 finished a descent on a lip under the sky that was not out of the ground, walked the opening, and cut stairs up to the top of the world until the filler was gone and the way down was :boxed. A perch (wood/perched?, under the sky, not out, not a pit) now descends toward a trunk at or below the feet (wood/trees-descend, wood/perch-down) before that climb (plan-test a-perch-under-the-sky-descends-toward-a-lower-trunk). Real-6 was already in that shaft, and each length's rim was the stair's own block a few above the feet, so the climb went on to y 124 with the sky open: the next length goes down toward the trunk (wood/trees-descend, plan-test a-shaft-under-the-sky-descends-toward-a-lower-trunk)."
  :problem/sources
  ["brain/bot/gotchas/drop-under-the-trunk.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/leaf-canopy-over-the-drop.md"
   "brain/bot/tooling/harness-landing.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/early-finish-aborts.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :kit
  :problem/issue 2
  :problem/goals [:kit]
  :problem/statement
  "Turn logs into a crafting table and four sticks through the 2x2 grid, believing only what the server says the window holds."
  :problem/needs
  ["The recipes, as data from the server jar."
   "Window 0 as the server sees it: grid, cursor and state id, separate from the inventory."
   "Which stack each ingredient comes from, chosen before the first click."]
  :problem/risks ["Leftover planks in the grid craft a button or pressure plate."
                  "A no-op click gets no answer and the craft stalls."
                  "The cursor model and the server's record of it disagree."
                  "A lost or lagged click leaves the grid dirty."]
  :problem/done
  "The server's inventory read shows a crafting_table and four sticks; the grid and cursor are empty."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Verified live on 26.1.2: after the put-back click the bot still believed a stack was on the cursor, clicked an empty slot to drop it, got no answer and failed :stale-window (fixed by dropping the cursor on every click, as the 775 server does). Sim race 38515210080 (issue #104, 19 runs, world R2/45) and race 38515209959 (4 real bots, the table in hand and the last intent its craft): the first log came down into a crevice of the forest floor two deep under its own canopy, and the sticks sent the bot for a second with the trunk two blocks off; a level step ran along the crevice's floor and the leaves over it are not cover, so stairs/out? said out, the one notch up ended under the leaves, no route reached a trunk or a hunt's ground, and it waited :no-log. The same false out as #102's quarry, fixed with it (stairs/pit-rim); plan-test a-crevice-under-the-canopy-is-climbed-out-of holds the crevice, and the snapshots of R2/45 under test/issues/104 the check. Played on (PR #114's issue check) R2-45-2 and R2-45-3 still failed: one stair up put the bot in a notch one deep under the leaves, every column round it had a cell to stand in a block up, so stairs/pit-rim took the notch for open ground, the climb ended and the wait began again. A step up needs the jump's headroom (stairs/step-rises): with leaves two over the feet no column a block up counts as stepped into, and the notch is still a pit. Issue #104 (R3-9-1) spent its only log on the table before the sticks, the climb back had nothing to pillar (:pillar :not-held) and the plan waited :no-log; the kit resolves the sticks first so one log leaves two planks to climb for the table."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/01-crafting-as-data.md"
                    "brain/bot/crafting/phantom-cursor-stale-window.md"
                    "brain/bot/crafting/junk-crafts.md" "brain/bot/crafting/sim-faults.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :pickaxe
  :problem/issue 7
  :problem/goals [:pickaxe]
  :problem/statement
  "Make a wooden pickaxe, which needs a 3x3 grid: place a crafting table where the server will accept it, open it, and craft through its window."
  :problem/needs
  ["A cell near the feet that is loaded, empty, supported and outside the player's box."
   "Whether the server accepted the placement (the block update), not the bot's own guess."
   "The table window's slots and state id once it opens."]
  :problem/risks ["No usable cell on uneven ground: placement fails :no-spot."
                  "Placing into the player's own box is rejected."
                  "A placement the server refused looks placed if predicted locally."]
  :problem/done
  "The server's inventory read shows a wooden_pickaxe and an execute if block at the table's position finds a crafting_table."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Recorded in CI: a pickaxe run on an uneven forest floor failed :no-spot because none of the twelve cells two blocks away was usable (fixed by searching rings 1 to 3, one up and one down, with an explicit body test). Recorded live 2026-10-10 and replayed: a table remembered 23 blocks away could not be walked to; three stuck walks failed the plan while the bot held planks for a new one (fixed: a blacklisted table no longer counts as near). Race 38477665442 bot Clj_r23 (issue #84, six real bots): the nearest cell held wildflowers, which the server's replaceable tag does not list, so the table was refused three times, :rejected; a spot is now air or a grass only, never a flower, and the model refuses the same. Race 38477665442 runner 10 bot Clj_r16 and the sim race in world R2/28 (issue #63, 348 sim runs): after the first log, walks to the trunks for the pickaxe's planks failed :no-path twelve times, the real bot in a hole under an oak canopy where every exit jump met leaves, the sim bot below a slope lined with one-layer snow a route took for an awkward shape, and both walked at trunks no route reached. Closed by d818567 (one layer of snow is clear to a route), 6449bdf (a trunk no route reaches is passed over) and 33ed30a (a pit under the sky has stairs cut up out of it); a-pocket-under-a-canopy-is-climbed-out-of and a-log-is-gathered-from-a-pocket-under-a-canopy hold the canopy case. Sim race 38515210080 at 7239df5 (issue #110, 13 runs, world R2/28): the table and four sticks made from the first two logs, the pickaxe's third plank sent the bot for a log and it waited :no-log on snowy ground with a trunk eight blocks off, every route :none over the one-layer snow; read at main the snapshot's near-walk finds that trunk's route (seven waypoints) and walks, since d818567 landed after the race. Its snapshots stay out of test/issues: the snowy world's 17,000 remembered logs make each half a megabyte, past the five the check allows; path-test a-snowfield-is-crossed-through-its-one-layer-snow holds the rule."
