 {:problem/stage :stone-tools
  :problem/issue 9
  :problem/goals [:cobblestone]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot can only dig a log by hand on a constant 3000 ms timer, so it cannot know how long stone takes, which tool to hold, that stone dug by hand drops nothing, or how to get down to stone without falling into a cave, lake or lava."
  :problem/needs
  ["Real block hardness per block, read from the game's own classes at datagen (the --reports output has none)"
   "Harvest rules: the jar's mineable/* and needs_*_tool tags (which tool kind, which tier)"
   "Which inventory slot holds the best tool, and the server-confirmed held slot"
   "Whether the eyes are in water and whether the bot is on the ground (each a /5 dig penalty)"
   "Liquid and air-column contents of every cell a stair-down step would open"
   "Remembered stone positions to walk to (memory watches logs only today)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Dig time too short: client predicts air, server restores the block with a block-update"
   "Held slot drifts from the server's, so the bot digs with the wrong item and the break is rejected"
   "Stone dug by hand or iron ore with a wooden pickaxe takes 7.5 s and drops nothing"
   "Tool breaks mid-run and later digs fall back to bare hand"
   "Digging under the feet drops the bot into lava, water or a deep shaft"
   "Reporting a dig-down as success when the bot never actually fell, so the caller spins"
   "Sim race 39550831606 R4/25 (issue #85) walked to the surface over its stone, which was the top of a birch's canopy, and every stair from there was refused for the leaves it opened onto, the walk back to the canopy repeating after each level step; the surface over stone is the highest solid block that is not leaves (stone/surface-over)"
   "Real bot Clj_r15 R1/30 (issue #65) was one stair down from a lake shore with two dirt, and the one water cell beside the next stair was never sealed, for the eight the climb back would need; a seal keeps the filler the climb back needs, a block for each block it is under the highest rock of its column, none at the surface (stairs/climb-reserve), and a mine boxed with under eight filler digs dirt for it first (stone/filler-dig)"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON Inventory shows at least 3 cobblestone with the wooden pickaxe still held, RESULT :ok true, and the recorded run replays to the same RESULT; crafting the stone pickaxe itself is left to the crafting issue."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Built 2026-10-10 (issue #9) against the model first: hardness, harvest tags and tool materials read from the game itself (stone has no tier, so a hand harvests it in 2300 ms, which the issue had wrong; a penalty divides the speed before ceil, 5650 ms not 5750); the dig chooses the fastest tool of the block's kind and refuses a tiered block no tool reaches; a refused break (the block restored after FINISH) fails :rejected; stairs down refuse water, lava and drops and never dig the support. The needs planner gained :goal/holds (a tool is required once, not per run) after it crafted three pickaxes for three cobblestone. Gym batch cobble-a1 (12 runs, set A): eleven timed out, the server logging 'lost connection: Timed out', because memory watched stone and held 120,000 sightings after ten chunks, so every chunk load and planner tick took seconds (fixed: exposed stone is the terrain's question, read from the loaded columns); the twelfth failed :no-path because six chunk arrivals each re-planned a found route (fixed: only a waypoint ahead gone unstandable re-plans). Batch cobble-a2: 10/12 pass, 44-93 s. Run 2 met iron ore four stairs down and the stair failed with the child's :needs-tool three times in a second (fixed: an undroppable cell turns the stair, like lava). Open, run 9 (landing 20480,19200): standing at y 73 on a hillside, the nearest exposed stone was at y 64 at the foot of a nine-block face; a cell beside it is standable, so it was chosen, but no route reaches it, and three such choices failed :no-path in a second. A stone target should be chosen only when a route reaches a cell beside it (plan before choosing), or stairs cut down instead. Found 2026-10-11 against the model (three-cobblestone): every stone collect waited out its 10 s and failed :not-picked-up, so three cobblestone took 63 s. The collect counted only logs; the walk ended on the surface two blocks above the stone, so the drop lay under the pickup box; and each failure blacklisted its stone, which hid that the stone search read the chunks without the overlay of the bot's own breaks (a dug stone was chosen again). Fixed: a collect counts its :intent/drops, a walk to stone ends where the stone is at the feet's height or up to two above them (path's :pickup goal; gym batch push70 showed one exact cell beside the stone can be walled off while a cell below it is reachable), and the search asks the overlay. Three cobblestone in the model now take about 11 s with no failed intent. ruststeve: placeholder hardness 1.0 made natural deepslate digs fail about half the time (the 1.35x+200 ms hold landed on the server's 70% threshold), and once both iron pickaxes wore out after ~550 digs, bare-hand descent ran ~44 s per block. Race 38477665442 (issue #42, 27 real bots and 674 sim runs a round): every bot landed in snow (runners 2, 6 and 10) cut its first stair into a snow block, which drops only to a shovel, and the staircase stopped :no-shovel for a tool it does not need, three times in a second. The stairs now stop only for a missing pickaxe; anything else is dug by hand. Same race, landing 2361,111,2361 (issue #65): a walk to stone stepped off a cliff, the dig failed :out-of-reach on the way down, and the staircase the mine started next was planned from the air, every heading refused for the drop, :boxed three times in the four seconds of the fall. A staircase now waits for the ground before it plans a stair. Same race, runner 9 (issue #59, and #66 at the ingots): with 25 bots on one server the acks of FINISH came 200-300 ms late and the breaks later or never (an early FINISH queued behind another and dropped), the dig ended on the ack alone with the cell overlaid as air, and the staircase walked into rock the server still had, put back by it ten times a second until the step timed out, :stair-not-taken three times. A dig now ends on the server's block update; its ack with the block still standing is :rejected, and the stairs dig that cell again. Race 38477665442 bots Clj_r19, Clj_r20, Clj_r11 and Clj_r22, runner 3 (issue #85): the stairs down for stone dug the block under the next step, the server acked the FINISH and never broke it, the bot's physics fell through the guessed air while the server put it back on the stone every tick, and the next dig waited to be still until the run timed out; a guess the server never answers is now forgotten after three seconds, and a dig starts after two seconds still or not. Race 38665691517 (issues #88, #144, #64): the server ran at 130 ms a tick and left standing the blocks the bot had finished digging by its own clock, three times a stair, :rejected; a dig now stretches by the server's tick length, read from the set-time packets (intent/slowdown). Race 39007359500 runner 5 bot Clj_r06 (issue #342) waited at furnace :boxed on a dry shelf after every descent refused side water, holding five cobblestone and twenty dirt; stairs down now seal supported side water before digging, without charging a seal over an existing floor against the cave-floor budget. Race 39110733219 runner 1 bot Clj_r15 (issue #65): the stair's last floor was one block wide, the bot stood on its rim with its feet cell open over a cave lake, and the collect for the stone it had dug walked off the rim into the lake; the nearest bank was a pocket it dug into until every stair and climb was refused, :boxed. A collect now stops on such a rim and leaves the drop."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/05-dig-with-tools-stone-pickaxe.md"
                    "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md" "brain/siblings/sib-dig-hardness.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-dig-stop-timing.md" "brain/siblings/sib-held-slot-drift.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-dig-down-safety.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :water-and-lava
  :problem/issue 5
  :problem/goals [:escape-water :escape-lava :shore]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot cannot tell it is in water or lava: liquids are passable air to the physics, nothing tracks breath, health or death, and the planner cannot interrupt a running intent, so a bot that walks into a pond sinks, walks the bottom and drowns without noticing."
  :problem/needs
  ["In-water, in-lava and eye-in-water flags written by the physics step every tick (eye at y+1.62, not feet+1)"
   "Fluid kind and level per block, from the block state ids"
   "Estimated air, fall distance, health-zero death and the respawn packet"
   "A bank to swim to: nearest column with air at eye height and solid support"
   "Water and lava sightings in memory, plus water-trap facts left behind after an escape"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["A swim pressed into the one water cell it would lay a bank into (the body covers it, so the server would refuse the block) backs off that shore and lays once the cell is free, instead of failing :stuck three times on a one-block bank (issue #351, swim/occupied-bank)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Jump in water gives almost no lift; only pressing into a bank fires the 0.3 wall impulse"
   "Swimming in an arbitrary heading goes deeper and drowns"
   "Head goes under mid-intent and the bot drowns inside the step"
   "A one-tick bob to dry Y reads as escaped, then the next step shoves it back in"
   "Roofed aquifer: every move goes up into stone while air is sideways and down"
   "Standing beside or over lava; a lily pad lid stops the rise"
   "Sim race 39005324315 R2/16 seed 1 (issue #339): a flee landed on placed cobblestone over lava but timed out :no-footing because floating-point support coordinates missed the integer-keyed block overlay; dry-land? must read the current floor with integer coordinates."]
  :problem/done
  "From a shore landing the bot walks into water and back out: RESULT reports :escaped true, RCON confirms no water at the feet or head cell and OnGround 1b, with at least 9 of 10 CI trials passing and zero deaths."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never attempted this. steve: the bot dove into cave water found 23 blocks down and was hard water-trapped in a 1-wide flooded pocket, losing the run (race81/192). ruststeve: rust-race-003 drowned in a water column under solid stone, every escape move going up while air was one block west and one down. Sim race 38659291345 world R1/1 (issue #148): sand had fallen round the bot at y 59 under a desert while it placed a block for the bucket, every cell beside it sand or sandstone under sand and no route anywhere, and the place failed :no-spot; a place with no route away now climbs a few stairs and looks again (place/fresh-rock). Race 38805758078 runner 1 (issues #156, #157) bot Clj_r44: a swim out of a flooded tunnel at y 16 toward a bank two blocks off at its own height, a block between at the feet, dug the ceiling over its head until nothing was named and failed :stuck; a wall at the feet under a level bank is now dug (swim/obstacle). Sim race 38844683780 runner 7 (issue #230, world R2/9): lava from a source ten over flowed into the pocket the bot smelted in, and the flee went to a cell the flow covered and timed out :no-footing three times; footing now takes only cells with no lava in, over or under them, those clear of its edge first (swim/footing). Sim race 38806318231 world R2/43 (issue #177, 83 runs): come up under a frozen sea, the bot dug the ice over its head, which the model broke to air, floated a block under the rim with no bank and timed out three times, :no-escape; the model now leaves water where ice is broken (sim/melts?) and the escape takes the ice as a bank (swim/bank?)."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/06-water-and-lava-survival.md" "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-water-traps.md" "brain/siblings/sib-water-escape.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-lava-safety.md"]}
