 a niche is now never under gravel or sand, and a chosen target the server fills before the click is given up for another. Race 38477665442 (issue #83, seven real bots): at beaches at y 63, three scoops each at sources the server acked and never filled; sugar cane grows on the sand by the water, and the game's ray for a bucket stops at its outline as at a wall. A source now needs air over it, not merely nothing solid, and every cell on the ray must be air or water. Race 38477665442 (issue #60, 19 real bots): four stood at y 6 at the bottom of one ravine, sixty under their landing with the sky open over them; the climb out applies under the ground alone, no hunt had a route, nothing lay to tunnel toward, and they waited :no-water out. Deep under the landing the bot now climbs to its height from a pit under the sky too, by stairs that end at that height alone. Sim race 38477665389 (issue #93, 45 runs, world R2/36 at y 83): gravel dug for flint at a ledge, its drop over the edge, and the collect's :ledge stop counted as a failure three times in a row, which ended the plan. A collect that meets a ledge now ends done with nothing, the drop left, and the row digs on. Sim race 38515210080 (issue #61, 104 runs a round, world R3/6 at y 37, and 44 real bots over three races): the bucket made, the climb out for water stood under an aquifer whose floor was two blocks over its head and over its own mine; every stair up was refused, :unsafe for the water over the cell it opened or for the step missing under its new feet, and the level steps, the top of every column being dry ground, went north under the aquifer and along the mine, a floor laid under each, until :boxed. A climb's level steps now head where nothing lies over the head, and a stair up lays its step from carried cobblestone as a stair down lays its floor. Race 38477665442 (issue #54, 14 real bots at y 55-72 holding a bucket; sim race 38477665389, 255 runs of R4/31): runner 8 bot Clj_r01 climbed out of its mine with the bucket through an aquifer, water beside every stair cell of the climb, each child dig refused :unsafe, the staircase was :boxed twice and twelve walks to that water failed :no-path. The sim reproduction (R4/31 seeds 1-5) scoops at a surface pond on 0ce899f, covered by the hunt over open ground, the pit climb and the snow layer of PR #101 (61cc9a2, 9e10a7f, d818567); the climb itself now seals the water beside a stair up with carried cobblestone before cutting it (stairs/seal, sim scenario stairs-up-through-an-aquifer-are-sealed-with-cobblestone). Sim races 38395033917 and 38477665389 (issue #73, 217 runs, world R4/44 at the flint and steel): afloat in an aquifer's lake under a cave roof, the eye in air, no cell within sixteen was standable (the rock walls rise straight from the water) and nothing solid lay over the head, so the escape held jump and looked again every second until it timed out, three times, :no-escape. With no bank the escape now notches the nearest wall, two cells over the water's top, and holds jump through a dig under an open surface, so the eye stays in air. Sim race 38515210080 (issue #95, 15 runs of R4/41 at the flint and steel, and four real bots of race 38515209959): the bucket filled, the bot was afloat in the column its source had left at the pond's edge, two under the bank, and the gravel to dig again for flint found no spot, three times in half a second, before the trap could preempt it. A place or a redig asked for with the body in water now gets ashore first, a swim-out for a retreat. Race 38515209959 (issue #103, 14 real bots at the furnace) and sim race 38515210080 (17 runs, world R3/36): the mine for the furnace's eight cobblestone dug the stairs it came down by, the bot stood at the bottom of its own quarry, two deep in the stone with a level step across the floor, and the furnace's table sent it for a log with the trees seven blocks off; stairs/out? said out, no route reached a trunk or a hunt's ground, and it waited :no-log. The same quarry as #102's, fixed with it (stairs/pit-rim); the snapshots of R3/36 go under test/issues/103 so the check holds. Sim race 38515210080 (issue #108, 56 runs, world R3/32): fourteen minutes in, the bucket crafted at the furnace down the mine, the climb out for the water wore the last stone pickaxe out in a tunnel at the surface (:no-pickaxe), and the new one's wood sent the bot back to the mouth of its mine, the quarry of its first cobblestone, two deep with a level step across the floor and the trees six blocks off; stairs/out? said out, no route reached a trunk or a hunt's ground, and it waited :no-log. The same quarry, the same fix; the snapshots go under test/issues/108. Race 38515209959 (issue #106, four real bots at the furnace): runner 9 bot Clj_r17 crafted its furnace and sent it to the same spot three times in two seconds, each answered with the cell still air and refused, :rejected; bot Clj_r24, landed at the same cell, was walking through that spot collecting the same drops, and the game places nothing into a player. A spot the server answers empty is now given up for another. The other three were a red tulip (Clj_r25, Clj_r12) and a niche placed into before the slow server had broken it (Clj_r02), fixed before (issues #84 and #64). Race 38515209959 (issue #105, four real bots :boxed at the flint and steel): runner 3 bots Clj_r19 and Clj_r13 and runner 9 bot Clj_r18 tunnelled for gravel at y 34-40 into underground water with 300-500 cobblestone in hand. Clj_r19 and Clj_r18 swam out of the water that came in onto a cell every stair and tunnel from which was refused, found no route away along the flooded tunnel, and waited :boxed out; Clj_r13 started three tunnels in a row from one pocket between two sheets of water, each :boxed a step or two on, and the third ended the plan. With no way away the mine now climbs out, eight stairs at a time, the stairs sealing the water beside them, and a tunnel that died :boxed is not started again from its pocket. Sim race 38515210080 (issue #109, 27 runs, world R4/3, landing 2744,1816,112, a mountain): at the bucket with five ingots and 354 cobblestone, both pickaxes worn out and the table lost (the walk back to it had failed), the bot at y 59 cut stairs up for the wood of a new table, and the climb stopped :no-pickaxe three times for the stone it would have dug by hand. A stair up is cut by hand when no pickaxe is held (1ce23ba, issue #40), and a worn tool is no spare (d22118b); two of the five snapshots are under test/issues/109 so the check holds. Race 38515209959 (issue #107, three real bots :stair-not-taken at the furnace, at 7239df5): bots Clj_r04 (runner 3) and Clj_r06 (runner 7), a collect jumping against a two-high wall, had their climb out asked for mid-jump at y 65.17, its cells planned a block too high, so the step under the new feet was never cut and the jump met the wall for 10 s, three times; bot Clj_r03 (runner 9) walked into a stair cell the lagging server had not cut, its FINISH dropped behind a delayed destroy, the ack alone having ended the dig. Covered since a54c3ec (a staircase waits for the ground) and ac38129 (a dig ends on the block update); the moment is held by a-stair-up-asked-for-mid-jump-waits-for-the-ground. Its snapshots hold the tick after the third place had failed, so the redig itself takes the retreat in place of a child that found no spot afloat, and starts the place again from the bank. Race 38650995686 (the first round that refilled each server's 25 bot slots the moment a bot ended, issue #132): crafts and smelt-side equips failed :stale-window on the first click left unanswered over 3 s, a loaded server's late answer read as a lost one. Every window intent now resyncs a lost click (window/lost) and fails only on the third. Sim race 38657453715 (issue #60): water seen with no route to it (a trench two under a pond's surface, ravine floors under remembered pools, a mountain ledge over them) left the hunt nothing but :no-water; it now cuts stairs up or down to the water's bank, or a tunnel at its height (scoop/to-bank). Sim race 38659291345 (issue #37): a climb for wood out of the mine stood under a lake (R4/38, half frozen over) and in a pocket under an aquifer's sheet (R1/33), every stair and level step bordering water, and failed :boxed; the climb now ducks a stair under the sheet (stairs/duck), never steps back onto a cell it stood on, takes ice for the lake it is, and a sim run knows its landing as a real one does. Sim race 38657453715 (issue #62): a staircase down a mountain met a lake and its level steps laid a causeway over the water until the cobblestone was spent, and every stair from it was :boxed for 75 minutes; a floor is never laid over a fluid now (stairs/over-fluid?). Race 38665691517 (issues #88, #144, #64): the server ran at 130 ms a tick and left standing the blocks the bot had finished digging by its own clock, three times a stair, :rejected; a dig now stretches by the server's tick length, read from the set-time packets (intent/slowdown). Sim race 38662908438 (issue #61, 115 runs): climbs for water under a lake or the sea were :boxed with the water in reach or over the head; deep under the landing the hunt now scoops a source it sees whatever is over it (scoop/seen-source) or digs up through a lake's bed and scoops from below (scoop/from-below), and a boxed climb out ends and is not cut from that cell again. Race 38674091115 runner 4 (issue #87): out of the iron mine at the mouth of its shaft under the open sky at y 70 with 999 trunks remembered and the nearest thirty blocks above on the mountain, the climb would not cut because out? said out and the hunt's band stops sixteen over the eye, so the plan waited :no-log; out is not at the trees, and a trunk remembered above the eye no walk reaches is now climbed toward (wood/trees-climb, to-height only, plan-test a-trunk-up-the-cliff-is-climbed-toward-when-out). Sim race 38669750355 (issue #69): landed on a hill, the cut down toward a pond and the climb out of the ground undid each other until the run's time ran out; with water seen the climbs give way to the cut toward its bank (scoop/scoop-next). Race 38759618225 runner 4 (issue #83, at 76010d2): four bots held the bucket and sent nine scoops each along lines within 0.03 of a block's edge, which the server's exact ray hit and the sampled one stepped past, and the side scoop chose the blacklisted source again; the ray now clears every cell within 0.03, the aim moves a quarter block off the centre when that ray is blocked, and blacklisted sources are left out. Sim race 38839767273 runner 6 (issue #69, worlds R3/8 and R4/35 at 3f836ff): the tunnel toward a bank walked an open corridor past its water and back, two thousand tunnels until the run's time ran out; a bank tunnel that ends no nearer its water now gives that pond up. Race 38842339863 runner 4 (issue #37, bots Clj_r01 and Clj_r08 at 3f836ff): the mine's stairs down ran along a cliff's face and a cave's wall, a floor laid before every stair with the rock a turn away, until the cobblestone the furnace left was spent and every stair was :boxed; a stair down now turns into the rock before it lays a floor (stairs/rock-heading). Race 38842339863 runner 4 (issue #37) bot Clj_r26: stairs down a gravel beach dug beside a gravel column standing on a cave lake; the beach dropped into the cave, the lake beside poured into the pit, and every stair from there was refused for the water, :boxed; a dig beside gravel or sand that rests on a fluid is now refused (intent/bed-over-fluid?), so the stairs go round it. Sim race 38844683780 (issue #230, world R2/9 at 74fa27b): lava falling from ten blocks up caught the bot smelting at y 38; it fled a cell, the mine chose the iron ore two blocks off under the same flow, and the lava caught it again until the flee found no footing, :no-footing; ore beside a lava trap still in force is now left alone, and beside one the mine retreats before any stair (path/near-lava-trap?, stone/exposed-of-states, stone/mine-next). Sim world R4/30 seed 1 (issue #69's second round): a bank tunnel that came no nearer gave up a pond it had just opened the walk to; a pond whose bank a walk reaches is now kept. Sim world R2/19 seed 12 (issue #87's second round): three walks to pools over a snowy mountain, routes of 123 and 175 waypoints, ran out of the flat sixty seconds short of their ends; a walk's deadline now grows half a second a waypoint. Race 38984748832 runner 3 bot Clj_r01 (issue #37, [:ingots :boxed]): the mine's stairs down broke into a cave at y 50 holding 16 cobblestone and 25 dirt, laid a floor under each of thirty-one stairs down through the open cave, and at y 19 stood on a one-block dirt bridge with none left, every stair refused; a stair down now lays floors only while the filler carried would reach its depth and keep 8 for the climb back (stairs/floors-affordable?). Sim race 38811426215 (issue #60, R4/29): a bot in the world's corner climbed its pit to the landing's height with pools 150 blocks off and below it remembered, no hunt with a route, and waited :no-water; a pool past pool-radius is now cut toward by stairs down or a tunnel (scoop/to-bank with far-pool-radius). Sim race 38900840841 (issue #62, worlds R1/31 and R2/46): the model never told a respawned bot the mobs again, so a zombie and a spider that followed it down the stair were unseen, :defend never fought them and it died on the same stair again and again until the 330 minutes ran out :timeout; the model now re-announces its mobs and items at a respawn (sim/retell-entities). Sim race 39070976103 R3/14 and race 39067023309 runner 8 (issue #151) placed gravel through a wall or round a corner and failed three collects :not-picked-up; redig now places only in a clear supported cell immediately beside the feet, or retreats to fresh ground before placing. Sim world R2/16 (issue #87): stairs cut up from the shaft's mouth at y 83 toward trees on a cliff ended on a ledge at y 99 that is not out of the ground, and the opening walked the bot back down to the mouth, where the climb began again every twenty seconds; wood/opening-up no longer walks to a mouth below the feet. Sim worlds R3/45 (issues #87 and #108): the bot climbed out of its pit on a pillar of its own cobblestone and stood eight blocks from the only trunk in reach across two blocks of air the path search does not bridge, and waited :no-log; wood/trees-bridge now cuts two stairs up toward such a trunk. The failed cross of the same worlds blacklisted the trunk and left the bridge nothing to climb toward; a failed :cross now blacklists nothing and counts against its trunk's column. Issue #342 (a real bot, Clj_r15, landed at R1/30): stone lay in the wall of a cave lake five blocks under its far bank, no route to it, and the mine cut stairs at the near bank among the water, boxed, up and down the same stairs until the plan failed :boxed; it now walks to the surface over the stone first and cuts the stairs there. Issue #342 (the R1/30 sim moment): the bot beside two stones of a cave lake's wall with water on their sides, three planks and no filler, cut stairs down and climbed out again in a loop until the plan failed :boxed; it now lays a block into that water first and digs the stone. Issue #349 (R4/2 and R2/44) laid its footholds, or stood where every cell had a drop beside it, and a stairs up that was already done repeated for fifteen minutes: the gravel now goes on the foothold (stone/hold-top) and a floor with a drop beside it but not past it is still a spot. Issue #171 (real-8) dug three cells beside the water it had just scooped, each :unsafe, and the plan ended; that cell is refused and the redig places again (stone-test a-redig-the-dig-refuses-as-unsafe-places-again-elsewhere). Race 40010178668 (issue #60): a bot on one cobblestone at y 63 with air round it tunnelled toward remembered pools, every step refused for the floor it lacked, each pool blacklisted in a tick until it waited :no-water; a tunnel now lays the floor a level step lacks, as a staircase's level step does."
