 {:problem/stage :portal
  :problem/issue 8
  :problem/goals [:portal-kit :cast-one :portal :nether]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot must cast ten obsidian blocks from lava and water into a nether portal frame, light it and stand in it, the way a player does: beside any lava pool at any depth, each frame cell a hole cut into the rock, lava poured in and water poured straight over it and scooped back, never mining obsidian (issue #124)."
  :problem/needs
  ["A site beside a lava pool whose frame, room and floors hold no fluid and touch none, with the lava's stand over the room's floor"
   "Loaded lava sources at any depth, a stand beside the cell over one, and the blocks the plan places where the rock is missing"
   "The server's block-update for every place and pour, never a local prediction"
   "Which ops of the build plan are already satisfied, so a resume skips them"
   "The current dimension, from the respawn packet"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A cast's water poured over the lava can land in the lava's own cell: the lava turns to obsidian, the water goes with it and the bucket stays empty, so the next cell's water pour failed :not-held (issue #455); the build's row asks the needs planner for a water bucket again (build/water-needed?). A lava source the digs' water turned to obsidian before the scoop aimed fails :target-gone; the refill chooses another (build/lava-gone?, issue #419)"
   "Sim snapshots R2-36-1 and R3-13-1 (issue #135) and R2-45-1 (issue #178) spent the judged window climbing to the surface for planks, deep in the rock with no pickaxe and every block of a stair dug by hand, 30 s a level: a climb out with no pickaxe held and a filler carried is now a shaft, one dig a level and a block laid under the feet (stairs/shaft?)"
   "A refill ray can cross the block supporting its own feet even when every lava cell is below them: reject that station and drop an in-flight refill dig of its support, rather than fall into lava and exhaust escapes with :no-footing (issue #228, R1/16 and R3/43)."
   "With no lava loaded at the sea's depth the hunt tunnels on, away from the landing, so new chunks load, rather than waiting :no-site (issue #41, real-4)."
   "A place whose retreat fails with the body afloat swims to a bank and looks for a spot there, rather than failing :no-spot in the open sea (issue #450, R3/34)."
   "A climb out over a cave's lake, the air over the head open and water beside it, pillars up (stairs/shaft-safe? asks the fluid beside only of a solid cell, a dig) and is not :boxed three times (issue #130, R1/26); a build out of the ground below its landing's height walks the level way, never the stairs up that end the tick they start (build/surface-climb?, issue #135, R2/39)."
   "A return portal (:nether) whose plain walk fails :no-path a second time gives that site up, the same as a cast-one: lava beside the stand is a cell a route never steps, and three failures of the one site end the plan (build/lost-way?, issue #561, R1/12 and R1/24). A :portal build holds a cast already made and is not given up for a walk."
   "Water from a later cast can flow through an earlier cell whose source was already scooped: cleanup must test for a remaining source, not any water, or it retries an uncollectable flow and fails :target-gone (issue #419, R1/20)."
   "The room's digs can let an aquifer in after the site was chosen dry: the floor row and the stands are awash and a route never crosses water, so the first wall op finds no stand and walks and digs fail :no-path or :out-of-reach three times; a build whose room holds water gives its site up for no stand, or a walk or dig that fails, a :portal build as a :cast-one does (issues #196, R3/40, and #461, R1/17)."
   "A climb out with no pickaxe pillars up a shaft (a level in 14 s by hand, deepslate) and must not give the shaft up for a swap into the hand's leftover send time (:no-answer) or a stack used up in the hand (:not-held with more in the pack): stairs cost twice a level (issue #178, R1-11-5); the deepest starts still outlast the 15-minute window."
   "A plant or vein (a sculk vein) in the cell before the cast's water stops the bucket's ray though nothing is built of it: the scoop of the water sent three times was never answered and the build failed :no-scoop on every try; the plant is dug first (plant-in-sight, issue #227, R2/15)."
   "A dig chosen at the edge of reach fails :out-of-reach a tick later as the walk's momentum carries the eye past 4.5: a block in the way of a stand is dug from inside reach with room to spare and walked to first otherwise (issue #461, real-5)."
   "Race 39088700340 bot Clj_r02 (issue #71) rose out of an air pocket under a frozen sea onto the ice and could not leave it: a route never stands on ice, so the mine cut stairs and laid floors on the sheet until it was :boxed; a bot on ice plans over it (path/on-ice?, stone/off-ice), and the rise up its shaft digs the ice cap and holds jump for the dig"
   "A boxed pocket whose search finds no waypoint (a cove between a cliff and a frozen lake, the feet on the ice) must still step to the standable cell the search began on, so the next descent starts from there and the plan does not wait :boxed to its end (issue #71, R2/35)."
   "Trees across water no route crosses: a grove is one failure, not a failed walk for each trunk, so the hunt and the crossing have their turn before twelve unwalkable walks end the plan (issue #75, real-1)."
   "A pocket under a powder-snow field has no air to put a table or furnace into, and powder snow is no place for a niche or a solid roof: cut the niche through it too, and place into the cell once dug, however a route could run through it (issue #94, real-2)."
   "Races 38999008545 bot Clj_r06 and 39060308623 bot Clj_r14 (issue #156): swim-outs and crossings blocked by packed ice spent three attempts on :stuck; escapes must drop banks left far below after progress stalls, clear overhangs and body-edge obstructions without removing a higher bank's step, and crossings must clear the same obstacles before continuing."
   "A bot in a dead end at under ten health backs away from a hostile it cannot get away from: a back-off that ran out its clock keeps its target (:plan/cornered) and :defend fights it to the end, rather than backing away every ten seconds for the run (issue #161, R3/41)."
   "A sea that meets a cliff leaning over the water leaves the cells a laid bank can use a block or two past the place reach: the escape swims along the wall to the nearest of them (wall-toward) before it falls back to a notch, which with no pickaxe takes 37 s a block and is no bank under a lean (issue #92, R4/9)."
   "A boxed cell with no retreat left must not wait :no-log out with the trees beyond the near band: the gather act ends in the climb the mine ends in (wood/way-out, stone/climb) (issue #89, real-3)."
   "A bot that rose out of a mine under the sea can stand on the one block in the water: every stair up is refused for the water and the climb dies :boxed there; the mine's last resort swims home to the landing (stone/cross-home) before it climbs (issue #71, real-3)."
   "A climb back to a distant portal site can exhaust every heading and fail :boxed: give up that site rather than spend three attempts on the same climb (issue #363, R2/43 and R4/18)."
   "A low source in a lava body extending above the feet may have no safe refill stand: skip it before tunnelling and when already beside it, rather than waiting :no-site with zero tunnel steps left (issue #392)."
   "At the lava sea's edge every source level or below the feet may be roofed in lava, the stand to open four blocks up: the hunt climbs to a source at most hunt-rise over the feet before it waits :no-site (issue #392, real-5)."
   "A bridge whose next gap lies past the reach of the place must walk onto the floor laid so far, not try the plain walk over the gap that has no route (issue #162, R3/43 and R3/44)."
   "After a site is given up, an adjacent source at the feet's level leaves a zero-step tunnel and must not hide farther lava the hunt can still advance toward (issue #392, R1/14)."
   "The lava bucket's last iron must not send retreats between boxed cells or back through failed searches: their visited cells must be remembered so a retreat reaches new ground (issue #161, R1/29)."
   "A reachable lit portal must be entered without reopening the casting room or gathering a replacement pickaxe and table: otherwise a completed portal can send the bot climbing through deepslate by hand for wood (issue #389, R2/38)."
   "Surplus deepslate and dirt can fill every slot while exactly 128 protected cobblestone remain: discard a surplus building-block stack while retaining 128 of its kind before gathering or crafting a replacement pickaxe (issue #382, R4/23)."
   "A broken pickaxe and no crafting table require wood below the feet: tree-directed stairs must be cut by hand, not repeatedly fail :no-pickaxe (issue #229, R4/5)"
   "A swim ends pressed to a one-block bank its lift peaks 0.05 under (63.95 against 64.0), the eye in air and no pickaxe to dig a step: it bobs there and every walk to a trunk on the cliff fails :no-path twelve times (issue #45, R1-17-2). A body off the ground over water for three seconds is trapped (trap/afloat?, a deliberate :cross or :wade excepted), and a swim-out stuck with nothing to dig lays a block into the water beside it for the step."
   "Trees near an exposed mountain ledge can require a long detour down the mine stairs: before waiting :no-log, search a larger bounded route and retain its budget through execution and replans (issue #186, R2/17)."
   "Lava pour lands outside the hole: the ray enters the frame below the cell (a stand too low or too far aside)"
   "Water poured beside the lava instead of over it: the source flows into the water and leaves cobblestone"
   "Water aimed at the floor replaces the lava source instead of making obsidian"
   "Scooping late lets water spread and convert the lava pool"
   "Gravel can fall into a lava refill's cleared ray while the bucket is equipped: drop the blocked scoop and reconsider the refill, rather than retry the stale aim until :no-scoop (issue #227, R3/26 and R3/29)."
   "Placing into a lava source destroys it; casting over a lava sea has no stance"
   "A refill approach through aquifer water or over solid magma is no walking route: require a firm walking floor, cut dry detours, and give up sites whose fixed stance or remaining refill stations are unusable, including on resume (issue #162, R1/16 and R1/42)."
   "A nearby dry build stance may still have no route from the feet: an exhausted fixed-stance walk must give up its site, including on resume, rather than retry the same pool until all attempts fail (issue #162, R1/17 and R3/23)."
   "A failed retreat walk toward one build site must not make every newly chosen site retry the same unreachable waypoint: remember that target in :plan/retreat-unreachable and recalculate the way out (issue #162, R2/43)."
   "Sim race 39032523584 (issue #231, R1/32): opening a low source's sight line admitted lava above the stand and three escapes failed :no-footing; stations and refills now reject ray excavations beside lava at or above the feet."
   "Sim race 39044511861 runner 6 (issue #380, R3/32): a stand's projected ray was safe but the slightly off-centre feet saw a wall holding back higher lava, so three refills failed :no-station; a station already occupied now checks the actual eyes and chooses another stand when unsafe."
   "A rejected placement left as a ghost block; the pathfinder digs finished obsidian"
   "A climb that opens a room floor for headroom must finish before the build repairs it: cancelling the climb on the changed op digs and replaces the same floor until cobblestone runs out (issue #369, R3/16)."
   "Lighting with the hitbox in the fire cell burns the bot"
   "Entering a lit portal from behind its protected back wall fails :no-path: approach through the room's landing when no route reaches the interior (issue #346, R4/1)"
   "A climb for portal wood boxed under gravel may have only a short way back: when no route reaches the retreat distance, walk to an unboxed waypoint instead of waiting :no-log (issue #370, R1/29)"
   "A climb out must not pillar up in the open air: its stairs are cut toward the nearest trunk, a bot afloat crosses to the trees before it climbs, a descent for the trees may lay its floor over water, and a perch no route leaves cuts a valley of stairs down toward them, on from each length's foot (issues #186 and #89, worlds R1/4, R2/29, R4/16 and real-2 Clj_r15)"
   "A descent for the trees that ends in the ground level with the trunk tunnels on toward it (foot-reach) rather than cutting stairs up to the top of the world and down again (issue #135, R2-43-1)"
   "A pickaxe broken in the cast or its child staircase exhausts the failure budget before replacement: the build must yield for held-first to replace it, retaining its site (issue #347, R1/35 and R1/4)"
   "A climb on a narrow ledge ducks through its own steps and fails :boxed with filler held: regain sound higher steps, reconsider an old duck before digging them away, and lay a holder beside the current floor before an unsupported step (issue #363, R1/35)."
   "Reconsidering a duck while only the previous floor's edge supports the body plans an ascent too high: require floor under the feet before reconsidering, and replan a rising step after falling below its launch height (issue #368, R4/20)."
   "Sim race 39007350790 runner 2 (issue #344, R3/4 seed 1): the sea bed dug beneath tall seagrass left water suspended over a dry shaft in the model, and three rises failed :no-escape; aquatic sources now flow, preserving their blocks, and older saved models wake sources beside changed cells once."
   "Sim races 39085720764 and 39085577169 (issue #130, R1/19 and R1/25): the lava hunt's tunnel was boxed in by an aquifer on every heading and failed :boxed three times in a tick toward one source; a boxed tunnel for lava gives its source up and ends, and none is cut again from its cell."
   "Real snapshots real-3-s2-Clj_r14 and real-7-s1-Clj_r13 (issue #41): at y -54 with thousands of sources loaded, none within the hunt radius, the hunt waited :no-site; the nearest source loaded, as far as the view shows, is tunnelled toward."
   "Sim race 39081492834 (issue #135, R4/34): in a flooded tunnel with the landing fifty blocks off, a gravel block on the straight way out of reach made every :no-path walk be dropped for a clear that never came; a build in water with no route swims out first, and only gravel in reach is a clear."
   "Real snapshot real-3-s2-Clj_r05 (issue #45): the staircase ended in the rock behind the frame, the feet's own cell the frame's rock, and no single corner was clear of it; a cast-one's plain walk that finds no path a second time gives its site up (a route of several corners round the box would keep it)."
   "Real snapshot real-6-s2-Clj_r05 (issue #45): the lava's stand was one block aside and one on from the feet with a stair floor the plan places between on the x-first line; the stance line takes the z-first way when a wall bars the x-first one."
   "Sim races 39076911005 and 39070979444 (issue #74, R3/22 and R1/38): six blocks from the landing at its height with rock between, the way back called itself near and gave none, :no-stand three times; a way is cut to the landing, and a cast-one with no stand gives its site up."
   "Sim race 39068773618 (issue #44, R4/37): the model refused cobblestone into a bubble column over magma, :rejected three times; the game's bubble column is replaceable."
   "A death at the site wakes the bot at spawn, far enough that the landing's chunk is not loaded: the build walks toward the landing first (build/far-way) before any stairs or dig, and a place or pour with no stance reachable goes back to the landing as a dig does (sim race 39076908669 runner 3, issue #196, R3/13 seed 2, 190 blocks off, :no-stand)"
   "The roof over a lava source is ore the held pickaxe cannot harvest: it is broken for nothing (build/way-dig), never refused :needs-tool three times (real race 39076909951, issue #163, deepslate diamond ore at y -59 under a stone pickaxe)"
   "A portal site no plain walk reaches three times in a row is given up like a cast-one's, the cast already there left for a new site (issue #162, R3-19-1: feet in water three blocks from the stand, :no-path three times in three ticks); a swim whose only bank is the dry floor under its water sinks to it, a stuck swim under a roof carves a notch and lets the search pick it, and a flee that finds no footing from a sunken body rises and looks again instead of failing :no-footing on the spot (issues #222 and #231)"]
