 {:problem/stage :nether-and-fortress
  :problem/issue 11
  :problem/goals [:fortress :return-nether]
  :problem/statement
  "The world value is overworld-only, so after a portal the bot cannot tell which dimension it is in, decodes Nether chunks with the wrong height, and has no safe way to reach a fortress across the lava sea."
  :problem/needs
  ["The dimension from login and respawn (sent as a registry index, 3 = the_nether)"
   "Per-dimension chunk height: Nether is min-y 0, 16 sections; overworld -64, 24 sections"
   "Sightings keyed by dimension, watching nether_bricks, spawner, portal, obsidian and lava"
   "Real chunk data after arrival before any step runs, not a timer"
   "Lava next to each tunnel step and missing floors ahead"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["With no brick on record a fortress tunnel sweeps a square spiral, not a line: legs of 160, 160, 320, 320 ... blocks a quarter turn right each, at y 52 to 90, a leg over at its end, at the world's edge, or after too many tunnels (issue #338: a line east went 630 blocks along the bedrock past a fortress 150 blocks north)"
   "A spiral leg that gains no ground is given up: three tunnels in a row (about four minutes) that bring the feet no 8 blocks nearer its end end it, and the next leg turns right or left to the longer run of rock ahead (a cavern sixty blocks across stalled R2/12 for twenty-eight minutes, eight pickaxes, 3 blocks a minute of net progress; issue #338)"
   "A target farther above or below the feet than aside takes the height first of every direction, not each direction's up, level and down in turn: a zigzag down to the bedrock under bricks 40 blocks overhead (issues #538 and #338, R2-25-2 and R2-6-2)"
   "A brick within 8 blocks horizontally and more than 3 above is climbed as a shaft, one dig a level and a block laid under the feet: a stair by hand is about twenty seconds a level, and forty-seven of them outlast the window (issue #338, R2-6-2)"
   "A target above the feet is climbed, even back up a stair already stood in, before a safe step down it: the only fresh safe step was down a cobble stair onto a 2x3 obsidian pad, and the pad refused every fresh step (issue #526, R2-29-1 and R2-36-1)"
   "A brick on record is tunnelled to with bridging on, as a stalled spiral leg is: a brick across a cavern was dug round at hand speed for a window (issue #338, R2-22-2)"
   "A floor step with no block to lay is given up and its cell counted visited, never placed with one not held; bastion bricks and soul sand are laid when no stone is (issue #410, R2-17-1 and R2-12-1)"
   "A stalled spiral leg floors a level step across a cavern when ground lies within 96 blocks under it (the lava sea is 30 deep, issue #538), 16 blocks are in hand and health is 14 or more: never over lava, water or the unloaded (issue #338, R2/12's thirty-block-deep cavern)"
   "A placement into a given cell the body clips at the edge first walks toward the middle of the feet's cell: the server refuses a block into any player at any overlap, and the same refusal came back at every try (issue #430)"
   "Chunks stay a snapshot of the dimension the bot is in, emptied on a change, as the server streams them again; memory keeps every dimension, each fact saying which"
   "A column's height is the sections the server sent (16 or 24), looked up in dimensions.edn: the reader thread decodes without knowing the dimension"
   "The dimension is the respawn's and login's name (:player/dimension, from #8), not the registry id, which only dimensions.edn's row order explains"
   "No lava capping: a cell behind a wall cannot be capped before the wall is dug, so a tunnel step never opens a cell beside lava and tries another step instead"
   "The gym gives a row's kit only once the server says the bot stands in the row's dimension (execute as <bot> at @s if dimension): steve gave its End kit before the cross-dimension teleport and the server held none of it (issue #261)"
   "A return-nether always row reuses the portal build after an overworld respawn while Nether targets remain undone; the first entry stays a historical milestone (issue #287)"
   "A build far from its site never digs stone by hand: past 24 blocks of the origin a lost pickaxe fails :no-pickaxe and the row makes one first, so a return to the portal after a death does not dig eighty blocks at 7.5 s each (issue #504)"
   "The sim model sets the overworld's columns and its placed and broken blocks aside when a portal or an end portal takes the player out of it, and a death in another dimension respawns over them again: before it a bot that died in the Nether stood in the Nether's columns at the overworld's spawn, saw no chunk and sat on stairs-down for hours, and its portal was gone (issue #504)"
   "A blocked tunnel considers a safe retreat and passes through portal cells without digging; fresh steps and a supported, non-fluid-floored corner onto adjoining ground precede revisiting a cell (issue #286)"
   "A tunnel replaces solid floors the route cannot walk, such as soul sand, before entering; the repair needs support and must expose no fluid or protected block, including when resuming a failed entry walk (issue #284)"
   "A route may leave the actual supported, clear feet cell on awkward footing without entering awkward waypoints; a tunnel retries an already failed entry walk only when a route now exists, rather than snapping from soul sand onto isolated neighbouring ground (issue #284)"
   "A descending walk stops input over its waypoint; a tunnel step counts only after centring and landing, then clears controls, so neither new nor in-flight steps run past their repaired floor into lava with no footing (issue #339)"
   "A tunnel never opens fluid-bearing gravel or sand beds above or beside its body cells; safety is rechecked before every body-cell dig and entry walk, dropping stale steps and their children to replan before lava leaves no escape footing (issue #339)"
   "A reachable dig works from the actual eye without demanding a new stance; when no working stance is reachable, a build returns to its landing's height even nearby instead of treating distance alone as arrival at the site (issue #328)"
   "A fortress tunnel digs a block out of its own body cells (gravel fallen in) before it chooses or works a step: no walk has a route from inside a block, and a step's entry asked one every tick for fifteen minutes (issue #338, R1-33-1)"
   "A tunnel at a dead end over a drop climbs onto a block laid beside its feet against the ledge before it retreats, the body on its footing while the block is laid, never a causeway; and a second retreat in a row into cells it already stood in is a pace, failed :blocked, not 32 steps counted a tunnel for four hours (issue #338, R3-6-1)"
   "A fortress tunnel replaces a lost pickaxe from held supplies before starting; a broken-tool tunnel yields without spending a failed attempt, and without replacement supplies even slow rock is cleared by hand rather than retrying no-pickaxe in the woodless Nether (issue #296)"
   "A tunnel stands ringed with lava (an arrival portal cast into a lava lake) only by capping the lava beside the cells a step opens first, a block placed into it from the stand, when a solid neighbour holds each and a filler is carried; and a body held by the edge of a block with the cell under its centre air steps back onto a standable floor beside it before it chooses a step (issues #286, #284)"
   "A step that lays a block (a replaced floor, a lava floor) is safe only with a filler carried, and soul soil, blackstone and basalt count as fillers: R3-38-1 dug a soul sand floor with none left and failed :not-held (issue #410)"
