  "clojurecraft has never attempted this. ruststeve: after entering the Nether its overworld columns answered Nether lookups (fortress brick reported 64 blocks too low) and the parser panicked on the shorter Nether chunk; finding the fortress was solved, but reaching it alive was not, with 9+ falls into the lava sea at one spot. Sim race 38999010135 (issue #328, R1/7 seed 2): after the portal the model resent the original columns without the dug room, putting the client's feet in deepslate and failing the first tunnel :no-stand; streamed columns now carry the model's changed blocks too, and fortress sightings use the indexed current-state query so the recovered tunnel can finish its judge window without scanning every sighting each tick. Issue #287 (R2/12 and R2/15 seed 1): Nether deaths respawned in the overworld with the Nether entry already reached, leaving only other-dimension waits; a return goal now works the portal again, and the model resets its dimension and resends terrain on that respawn. Issue #328 recurred in R1/1 seed 2 and real-6-s1-Clj_r09: a reachable tunnel dig demanded a clear centred stance, while a return build five blocks above its landing could neither reach a working stance nor pass the distance-only return gate. Digs now use the actual eye's reach, and a build with no reachable stance returns to its landing's height even nearby. Issues #341 and #352 (for #338 and #351): the sim race's portal kept the overworld's columns, so a sim bot \"in the Nether\" tunnelled overworld stone and aquifers for bricks that were not there; every sim-only fortress failure was the model's. Issue #353: each race set's real Nether is captured once (capture_nether.clj) and a sim run's portal leads into it, the player where the server would link the portal (sim/arrival), the columns streamed round it as a server's view. Sim races 39085649638 and 39081492834 (issue #410, R1/34 and R2/39): tunnel floors spent all cobblestone with other safe filler still carried, then failed :not-held; each floor op now selects carried filler and replaces a stale placement child when that material changes. Sim race 39095704051 and 39099976057 (issue #338, R2/4, R4/33, R3/13, R3/21 at 995b9c1): a tunnel with no brick on record aimed 48 blocks east for ever, drifted down a block whenever its level step was refused, and ended on the bedrock or at the east edge of the captured region, 630 and 700 blocks from where it entered, with fortress bricks 150 and 310 blocks to its north and south; and in a cavern every step ahead was an air floor, refused, so it paced a ledge for half an hour at a time. The search is now a spiral (fortress/exploring); four seeds each reach the fortress in R4/33, R3/13, R3/21 and 3 of 4 in R1/43, where main reached none. Open: R2/4 and R2/5 have no brick within 300 blocks of their landings (the nearest 310 and 337 away, capture_nether bricks), the spiral takes hours to reach one, and in a cavern every step ahead is an air floor, refused, so the tunnel paces a ledge for half an hour at a time; bridging the floor toward the target made R3/13, R3/21 and R1/43 worse, and ending an idle leg gained nothing (brain/bot/plan/fortress-tunnel.md). Race 39095700271 runner 3 bot Clj_r04 (issue #430): the stairs out of a flooded pocket sealed the water beside the feet from x 2838.74, 0.04 over the edge of the cell, refused three times, boxed; the place now steps off first. Sim race 39113082582 (issue #339, R3/33): a fortress tunnel dropped gravel with lava beside it higher up the stack, flooding every escape footing; the falling-roof check now checks every face of the stack, so new and in-flight steps leave that bed sealed and replan. Sim races 39593212933 and 39597574132 at 33c3dfc (issue #338, R3/6 and R2/12 seed 1, both timeouts at 330 minutes with no brick ever seen): R3-6-1 stood from minute 90 on two blocks of a ledge at y 39, seven over the lava sea, every way round them air, and paced the two cells, each retreat counted a step, 32 a tunnel every fifteen seconds, the spiral turning on the spot (1,134 intents); the tunnel now climbs onto a block laid beside its feet against the ledge (fortress/climb-out?) and a second retreat in a row fails it :blocked. R2-12-1 was no pace: its pickaxe worn out with one stick and one plank left, it tunnelled a basalt delta by hand at 7.5 s a block, 15 s a step, 8 minutes a tunnel; a spare pickaxe's wood carried through the portal is left open. Measured on sim snapshots (issues #338, #286, 15-minute windows): R2-4-2 and R2-12-2 held no pickaxe (one stick and one plank, a table in the first), dug by hand at 11 s a step, and stayed 250 and 264 blocks from the nearest brick (a leg's end 610 blocks away) the whole window, 13 blocks net and none; R1-35-1 and R2-3-1 held none either but went straight, 9 and 5 blocks a minute, 415 and 126 blocks short, which is longer than the window. R2-39-1 (y 20 under a brick at y 55) and R3-23-1 (a cobblestone patch over the lava sea) fail :blocked in a pocket of cavern floor: ten of twelve steps are an air floor or beside lava, and the two safe ones are the cells just left. Trying the steps up before any step down (a target more over than aside) turned R2-39-1's :blocked into thirty minutes of pacing the same floor at y 20-21, so it was not kept. Traced on sim runs from spawn (probes 39778484412, 39782256061, issue #338): a stone pickaxe wears out in the Nether's tunnel in about two minutes and 65 blocks (R3/29 seed 2: 84, 60, a new one at 130, 62, none), the fortress is 250 to 630 blocks off, so the tunnel makes four to ten pickaxes of two sticks each; the bots came through the portal with 1 to 3 sticks and one pickaxe of 15 to 34 uses left or none, and R2/12 seed 2, R3/29 seed 2 and R2/3 seed 1 left the table standing (at the portal's last pickaxe, and at the tunnel's first) with sticks and 250 to 937 cobblestone in hand and no wood for another; the iron row's :goal/spares of 24 sticks (was 4) carries 17 to 23 sticks through the portal (probe 39846994607: R2/12 made 8 pickaxes over 36 minutes); the build's own kit is asked underground, where no trunk is near, so it never fires (probes 39845006016 and 39846165059 came through unchanged). This change: the iron row keeps 24 sticks, the build takes the placed table along on the way into a lit portal, and the tunnel takes it along once its pickaxe is made. A bot already in the Nether with sticks and no table, or a table and one stick, has no way to a pickaxe in the woodless Nether: R1-12-1 and R3-29-2 hold two planks, three sticks and 600 to 800 cobblestone. Probes 39855333521 and 39856649219 (fortress8): R3-28-1 held 671 basalt and failed :inventory-full at its table (basalt, blackstone and magma blocks are now thrown from a full pack); with sticks R2/12 seed 2 still wears a pickaxe out every three minutes in one cavern, 130 digs for 10 to 15 blocks of progress."
