  "Not played yet: the parts land first (issue #262): a drop's stack is read from its metadata, :collect-drops is done when nothing of the item lies near, a Nether spawner is remembered, and an engaged fight walks on toward a target hovering out of reach. Then the goal (blaze.clj) and its gym rows: blaze-1 (invulnerable, six rods given) passed 3/3 twice (runs 38891907112, 38893160457). blaze-7 (not invulnerable) died twice of three burning in a 7-square room (blaze-7a, run 38891910129) and stalled once when fire by the spawner lit its floor past light 11, so the spawner made no blaze for three minutes: the arena now sets mob griefing off and gives Fire Resistance; then 2/3 (blaze-7b), a volley taking 12.7 health in two seconds while the bot fought on hungry (a meal now comes first under 14 health); then 3/5 (blaze-7c), three blazes' volleys at once killing from 16; with one blaze at a time from a slower spawner, 5/5 (blaze-7d, run 38896099962), breaking off under 10 in three runs and eating in four. blaze-fortress (from the fortress pad): every run failed three fights :unreachable on blazes seen through the fortress's walls (blaze-fortress-a; only reachable blazes are fought now), then camped ten minutes in the wall four over the spawner, its blazes out of reach (blaze-fortress-b; a tunnel to a spawner now ends in the open cell beside it, climbing first); then came up three under the spawner's floor and killed eight blazes whose rods lay out of reach over it, while the :defend row chased blazes through walls and over its head (blaze-fortress-c; only blazes in sight and within 3 over or 2 under the feet are fought now, by either row); then reached the cell beside the spawner and died there waiting to heal, burning and shot, in every run of -e, -f and -g (a hurt bot now hides in the nearest cell out of a watching blaze's sight, and the row gives Fire Resistance); blaze-fortress-h (run 38905665758) still 0/3: fights :unreachable three in a row (the fight's approach walks straight, never along a route, and a blaze behind a fortress fence is never reached), the tunnel's step into the spawner's room failing :no-path, and one run slain by volleys. With the slower arena spawner blaze-7 passed 14/15 (blaze-7d, -e, -f) and blaze-1 3/3 in every batch. A fight now approaches along a route once the straight way stalls, engages when the route says it stands as near as it walks, and a tunnel step the feet left is chosen again: blaze-fortress passed for the first time, 2/3 (run 38911617612) and 1/5 (run 38913023560); the rest died to volleys from the natural spawner's bursts, failed fights :unreachable, or timed out at another landing's fortress. blazefort-k (run 38913023560) 1/5: runs 3 and 4 died at the spawner from over 14 health in four seconds, a hit of 3.12 a second from the natural spawner's burst, one camping on through it (nothing ends a running intent but itself), one fighting on at 11.5 while watched and then eating at 9.4 in the open; run 1 failed three fights :unreachable, run 5 timed out at another landing's fortress. A camp and the new :rest now end when the health falls; a bot watched by three blazes takes cover whatever its health, a wary one (under 14) before its next fight and a hurt one before its meal, the cover a cell out of every watcher's sight; a camp is only where the spawner's top is in sight; a fire by the spawner is put out. blaze-fire-a (run 39131023637, at b805035) 1/5: run 1 opened its tunnel into the spawner's room as a burst came, six blazes within five blocks hitting in melee, and the :defend row (which answers anything within 4 before this row is asked) fought them from 20 health to 7 in four seconds and died backing away; runs 2 and 4 failed three fights :unreachable in four seconds from the end of the tunnel, on blazes a walk's route came within three of while the fight's own route, within two, found none; run 5 timed out on the other landing's pad (2144,1760), the tunnel finding no safe step down and walking the ring it dug round the pad for half an hour; run 3 passed. The :defend row now leaves blazes to this row while it is worked (combat/answers), a fight is chosen only where the fight's approach comes to it (combat/approachable?, a hovering blaze's cell brought down to the feet's floor), and this row's fights end under 10 for its cover, meal or rest instead of combat's straight retreat. blaze-fire-b (run 39136853644, at 6c0331e) runs 3 and 4 died in the tunnel's mouth: blazes at hand followed the bot into cover after cover (a blaze flies to where it last saw its target and hits in melee within two) and it died from 14 health without a swing, after tunnelling on with one hitting it from 20 to 13.8. A blaze at hand (within 4) is now fought first and to the end, whatever the health, and ends any other running intent (plan/interrupts?). blaze-fire-c (run 39152583546, at bfe3cb6): blaze-fortress 4/5 from the fortress pad with the natural spawner (Fire Resistance and iron armour given; no mob griefing off, no slow spawner), every run at the 2288,2304 landing passing; run 5 timed out on the 2144,1760 landing, a five-square pad floating in an open cavern with air under its floor, where the tunnel (fortress/safe?: never a step over air) finds no way down and walks the ring round the pad. blaze-7 2/3: run 1 fought each blaze the slow spawner made at hand to the end and died at under 5 health, where it used to back away and heal."
