  "Not played yet: the sim lanes ran without hunger or mobs while the real races ran at Normal (#257), so a death or an empty bar was a real-only failure. Hunger landed first (PR #270: the bar drains at Normal in every sim lane run); then mobs (night and dark spawns, melee, arrows, creeper blasts, the 775 attack with its hurt window, loot), so a lane run now dies to a zombie as a real one does (mob_test the-bot-killed-by-a-zombie-respawns). Then eyes of ender flown toward :stronghold, frames that light the end portal, and the End (the platform, a perched dragon of 200 health its crystals heal), so the stronghold, portal and dragon stages can be played against the model first (end_test). Then the Nether's own spawns (issue #263): the model spawned hostiles only in the overworld (spawning? held only overworld?) and a fortress's spawner was the Nether's only spawning, so a sim run in a captured Nether met no enderman and the sim race stayed at blaze-rods while the real race was raised to pearls-12 (#516). Vanilla spawns the Nether's hostiles by biome, a warped forest's list being the enderman alone in packs of four; the captured bytes carry the biome containers but chunk/read-section keeps the blocks alone, so the model tells a warped forest by its floor, warped nylium, as the bot does, and try-nether-spawn rolls a column in the ring, a nylium spot with three cells of room, and a pack walked out from it as NaturalSpawner does, from the Nether's own roll stream (wild-roll) so the overworld's nights roll as before, and a Nether run with no warped forest rolls its fortress's blazes as before (mob_test a-warped-forest-spawns-packs-of-endermen-by-day-and-netherrack-spawns-nothing). Probe 39779112668, the bot put in each set's warped forest with an iron kit: packs spawned in every set, R4's hunt took six pearls in eight minutes then failed :unreachable on a drop, R1-R3 took none in an hour (most likely as the model's endermen neither path round walls nor teleport, so a provoked one beyond a wall never comes); in a flat nylium arena at Easy a pack killed the bot in its :defend fight (test.yml 39778621263), so no whole-bot pearl test is kept yet. Not modelled: the other biomes' hostiles, and the biome itself (netherrack patches in a forest spawn nothing, shroomlit cells spawn as dark ones). 2026-10-22, issue #263: an angry enderman now walks a route round what stops its straight walk (sim/trail, mob/route: a breadth-first search of 1024 cells, three tall, drops of three, ending nearest the player as vanilla's partial path does, so a tunnel two high still keeps it at the mouth) and teleports as EndermanLookForPlayerGoal makes it: toward the player after 30 ticks farther than 16 (mob/toward-aim), away when stared at within 4 (mob/away-aim), landing on a floor with three clear cells (mob/landing); its rolls come from mob-roll and only an angry enderman's teleports spend them. Not modelled: its teleports out of water, rain, daylight or a non-living hurt. Probe 39847287615 (probe/263-sim-teleport, the same pearl probe on this model, seed 3, 60 simulated minutes): R4 took its twelve pearls in 23 minutes (21 provoked, 21 killed); R1 and R2 took nine each (22 and 23 provoked, 21 and 22 killed), against none before; R3 one (3 provoked, 2 killed), its last angry enderman stuck 8 blocks off where no route nearer exists (5,740 empty searches). The first death in R1, R2 and R4 (t 1421, 835 and 1240 s) was each time an enderman the bot provoked at 10.8 to 17.8 health just outside its burrow, hitting it three to five times with a clear line within five seconds (probe 39848524906 logs every hit): the bot's fight, not the model."
