wn stairs and tunnels with 21 digs left, its second flight down having taken the floor of its first flight's third stair; run 3 on a ledge over a pit with 208 digs, every enderman past cut-reach. The hunt now cuts its way out toward the nearest enderman when the roam finds no end (dig-out), along the heading whose first cut digs least (cheapest-heading). Run 1 walked from its burrow to the mouth and back every 34 s for four hours over an angry enderman 4 blocks from the mouth, blacklisted after a held fight timed out :unreachable, that never came (angry-near holds the burrow from going stale, and the lure brought nothing); a blacklisted angry one now counts only until lure-tries lures (lured-out?). Gym batch pearls-warped8-b (plan run 39775345028, the mouth fix; probes 39848848462, 39849820209): pearls-12 0/3, 1, 3 and 1 pearls, two runs dead: run 3 at 6 minutes, out at its first stair with the walk home failing :no-path, stood in :lookout while an angry enderman killed it in three seconds (the walk home is now taken only with a route, else one coming at hand is fought); run 1 at 24 minutes stood in a fire lit on gravel where its walk ended, in :lookout, until dead (a fire at the feet or head is now put out first, burning-at); both then respawned with nothing held and hunted bare-handed, 39 and 26 deaths in five hours (no sword held now fails the plan, :no-sword). Gym batch pearls-warped8-c (plan run 39845223845, dig-out; probe 39854206523): run 2 had 3 pearls at 16 minutes when dig-out's stairs up started on a ledge over a lava lake and the stair's lay backed the bot off the edge into the lava (:no-footing); dig-out now cuts from no brink (brink?). Sim-endermen3's probe 39847287615 (teleporting endermen, PR #542): the first deaths in R1, R2 and R4 came of provokes 4 to 8 off at 10.8 to 17.8 health just outside the burrow; no enderman is now provoked under provoke-health, and from a vantage only at full health. Round 9 (sim probes 39883381560, 39883402083, 39883422507, teleporting endermen, seeds 3 to 5): worlds R1, R2 and R4 stood 28 to 49 of 60 minutes in lookouts in a burrow whose mouth a calm enderman crowded, too near to stare at from the mouth and hidden from the end; each minute the burrow went stale and the walk toward that enderman and the burrow cut beside it were the old burrow again (the sim's calm endermen never move); a stale burrow over a crowder now walks to a site a new burrow stares at it from (crowd-site). The lay that backed run 2 into the lava is refused in stairs.clj itself (backs-off?), for every climb and descent. Sim race 39909643851 (issue #563, world R3/13 seed 2) broke its stone sword with cobblestone, a stick and a trunk two blocks off, and the plan failed :no-sword: the sword row stays done without a table at hand. With no sword held the hunt now makes the sword the held items pay for when that craft can start, and still waits :no-sword when it cannot. Probe 39962668627 on that fix died in the open: the stone sword had nine swings left and was fought until it broke, and once a log was laid into the grid (make/counts sees the inventory alone) the sword row dropped the craft for another trunk. A sword under spare-uses swings is made again before the fight. Probe 40017786878 still hunted first and died once: make/counts treated the worn stone sword as the one the row provides, so no craft started until it broke; the bot then crafted, took a pearl and ended at full health. The worn stack now keeps its slot and is not that sword, and a log in the grid keeps the row on the craft. Probe 40022662598, after merging main, crafted that second stone sword and did not die in the window, then hunted: the sword craft at t 13838700 was preempted back to the lookout and the fights left 1.3 health, so the next enderman hit still kills. Under danger-health (one hit plus a margin) the hunt now backs off, goes home, eats or rests instead of fighting, provoking, walking toward an enderman or crafting, and the burrow's held fight yields at that line. Batch pearls-m10-a (plan run 40106206590): run 1 timed out in lookouts with no route reaching a roam-goal (roam now goes as far as the route goes when none reaches); run 2 took 6 pearls from 12 kills and failed :no-sword with 8 warped stems held (wooden sword now crafted from stems when none payable); run 3 provoked an unreachable enderman down a ledge within 16 blocks that could not path to the mouth and never teleported, the held fight blacklisted it, lures timed out and the bot walked into the open and died to lava (an enderman under 16 blocks is provokable only when a route reaches the mouth or feet; a lured-out burrow cuts out the other way when an angry one stands near the mouth; a pickaxe held only walks to a stare-site and never charges at distant angry endermen in the open). Batch pearls-m10-b (plan run 40131980094) disconnected every run in seconds: a path/plan spec bug (a bare position vector where a goal map belongs) crashed the bot, fixed before the next batch. Batch pearls-m10-c (plan run 40133706786): pearls-1-live 3/3, pearls-12 0/3 again; run 1 held 3 pearls at the five-hour timeout, and runs 2 and 3 died at 358 s and 1400 s, each death followed at once by the :no-sword wait on empty hands. The round since: a distant angry enderman with a pickaxe held is met standing (a held, yielding fight), not charged and not merely looked out for (the lookout stood the hunt still while any angry one was tracked); the cut out of a burrow is kept only for one standing in its stairs, never for one merely lured-out near the mouth, and angry-near counts blacklisted ones as before; and empty hands ask for a wooden sword from a remembered trunk or the log hunt, so a death no longer fails :no-sword on the respawn. Batch pearls-w1 (plan run 40387599204; the sim gate first, probes 40384292887, 40384331138 and 40384356540 against main's 40384395700, 40384417922 and 40384440835: pearls and deaths 111/25 against 104/51 over seeds 3 to 5, done 8 of 12 against 6): run 3 passed pearls-12 for the first time, twelve pearls in 5264 s and no death, and pearls-1-live passed 3/3; run 1 went up in flames in the caves under the floor at y 37, having dug out the fire in its feet's cell while its box still overlapped the fire on gravel in the cell north, and stood in :eat and :lookout burning for twenty seconds (probe 40421394796 folded its recording at 380813e); respawned at the overworld spawn it remade a wooden sword, then failed :no-pickaxe with sticks and its table held. burning-at now covers every cell the body overlaps, and with no pickaxe at all the log hunt may start the remake, as it may the sword's. Run 2 of the same batch held five pearls and no death at the five-hour timeout: from 21:41 it walked between the roam ends [2474 63 2168] and [2487 63 2168] 1,443 times, a lookout between, each the farthest spent end the roam's revisit found from the other, its last fight at 21:55. The revisit now refuses the two ends the last walks arrived at (memory/newest-dones), so a two-end pocket digs out or rests instead of ping-ponging. Batch pearls-w2 (plan run 40428200343, at e2b790c with the burning and log-hunt fixes) run 3 was slain by a piglin at 110 s after walking fifty blocks south out of the forest and fighting two of them, then respawned, remade its wooden sword and failed :no-pickaxe again by 184 s: spruces were remembered at its spawn, so the planner asked for the trunk (:log), and the remake gate refused that walk while the table's pieces were held - the taken-up table itself counts (sword/pieces?) - with no plank and no log held. The sword and pickaxe remake gates now refuse a trunk walk only while a log is already counted in hand or in the grid (log-counted?). Run 2 of the same batch died at 2120 s to an enderman, respawned at the overworld spawn, remade its wooden sword, and began making a pickaxe: fetching wood for it called make/take-table, and after digging up the placed table, collecting the dropped table item (intent/chain-next with :intent/kind :collect :intent/for :take-table) was refused because pick-acts had no :collect, leaving the bot waiting :no-pickaxe on the respawn. pick-acts and sword-acts now include :collect. The piglin death is still open."
