 {:problem/stage :stronghold
  :problem/issue 265
  :problem/goals [:eye-throw :stronghold :portal-room]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. Find the stronghold from the overworld with eyes of ender and reach its portal room: throw an eye and follow it to read the line to the stronghold, throw a second from somewhere off that line, cross the two lines, go there, and get down to the room whose twelve end portal frames the End needs. The one stage of the run no sibling has proven."
  :problem/needs
  ["The eye's entity: the add-entity of type eye_of_ender (50) that follows the bot's use-item, at its middle, and the moves the server tells of it (the mob model keeps every entity, #258)"
   "Where the eye was a moment after it was first seen: the line to the stronghold on the plane"
   "A crossing of two lines that answers nothing when they are parallel or cross behind a throw"
   "The eye that drops as an item, four throws in five, where its flight ended, picked up again (#262's :collect-drops)"
   "Where the portal room is: the end_portal_frame blocks in the chunks loaded round the crossing, remembered as landmarks"
   "A way down to it through stone and the stronghold's walls: the fortress tunnel's step plans"]
  :problem/risks
  ["An eye shatters one throw in five, and twelve are wanted for the frames: every throw spends from the portal's budget"
   "Two throws along one line say nothing about how far: the second must be thrown from off the first line"
   "A use-item while looking at a block uses the block: looking at an end portal frame fills it instead of throwing"
   "The eye flies only in the overworld: in the Nether or the End it is not thrown at all"
   "A walk of hundreds of blocks to the crossing over oceans, ravines and mountains"
   "The stronghold under an ocean or an aquifer: water on the way down"
   "Silverfish in the stronghold's infested stone bricks"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["The second throw is made from a point stepped off at an angle to the first line: thrown from along the line it is the same line, and triangulate's parallel case answers nothing"
   "A throw is a fact on the world (:stronghold/throws), kept across deaths: what the eyes said stays true"
   "The rows are asides until the eyes (#264) are proven and the chain is raised to them, so plan/current-until stays the fortress"
   "The frames are in the chunk data as soon as their chunk loads, so the room is found from memory, not by walking corridors; the way to it is the fortress tunnel's"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON: a throw's line within 10 degrees of locate structure minecraft:stronghold from where it was thrown (gym throw); an end_portal_frame at the cell the bot remembers one after two throws (gym stronghold); the bot within 6 blocks of a frame (gym portal-room)."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never thrown an eye. steve's find.ts is a stub (\"TODO: Track the eye entity, calculate direction, triangulate\"), it throws one eye and reports success after 3 s; ruststeve never got past the blazes' rods to need one. Gym batch stronghold-265a (plan run 38927120252): the throw row passed 5/5, every line within ten degrees of the stronghold locate found 6000 to 8300 blocks off; the stronghold and portal-room rows, landed 250 blocks from it, failed 0/6 in three minutes: two landings on a lake's shore had the stronghold across the water and every hop toward the second throw's spot ended in it, one on a mountainside walked at one cell twelve times; each waited :no-way (probe 38929010443). The way now swims open water (swim's :cross) and tunnels where no route goes, and the second throw is made once 32 blocks off the first line. Batch stronghold-265b (plan run 38930188463): the stronghold row passed 2/3, a frame at y 0 remembered under the lake both times; the third, in a pale garden on a mountain, stood with its step's walk making no way into a cell of moss carpet, :no-path (open); the portal room 0/3: the frame seen while swimming the lake, the tunnel from the water :blocked (the bot now leaves the water first, and stairs down where no tunnel step starts), and four eyes picked up from a tree six over the feet :not-picked-up (an eye is picked up only within two of the feet's height now). Batch stronghold-265c (plan run 38934412014): the stronghold row 2/3 again, the pale garden :no-path again; the portal room 0/3: run 1 stuck in the lake (the swim across to the crossing fought a drowned, the swim out to the bank failed :stuck three times two blocks from it); run 2 out of the lake onto its bank over the frame, where every stair's cells bordered water, :boxed three times; run 3 over the mountain tunnelled from y 120 toward the frame at y -16, level wherever the floor under the next cell down was air (a tunnel never steps onto air), stood over the frame at y 84 with a cave under it and stepped level between two cells 32 steps a tunnel for eighteen minutes to the timeout. The recording of the pale garden showed 2021 teleports and no step in three minutes: the feet stood on pale moss carpet, a sixteenth of a block the bot's physics collided with as nothing, so the server refused every move of a body inside it. Now: carpets collide as their flat box and are stepped onto (blocks/collision-top, physics/rise-onto); from a shore the way down starts at a dry cell (dry-start); from more than 8 over the frame the way down is the stairs, which lay a floor over a cave, a leg of 8 at a time toward it, to a block over the frame; the tunnel the last blocks, and the stairs again after a tunnel that took every step without arriving. Batch stronghold-room-a (plan run 39131390440): the stronghold row 3/3 (the pale garden passed); the portal room 1/3, run 3 over the mountain in 980 s, runs 1 and 2 by the lake :boxed. Batch stronghold-room-b (plan run 39132210882): run 1 swam out to the lake's east shore, staired down 56 and tunnelled 200 blocks under the lake to the frame; run 2 ended its swim toward the crossing on a block in the lake over the frame, nothing dry within 48 of it (probe 39134431529), every stair from it into the water, :boxed. Now: with no dry start within 16, a swim to the nearest dry cell farther off (far-start, out to 80), else back to the ground last walked (walked-ground). Batch b's run 3 over the mountain timed out: its stairs went down through a cave to the frame's height 126 blocks from it, nothing solid for 12 blocks round but its own stair floors (probe 39137426809), every tunnel step toward the frame over air, and it walked its own stairs 32 steps a tunnel for 23 minutes. Now the dry tunnel floors its way across a cave from the filler carried (fortress/bridge?). Batch stronghold-room-c (plan run 39135557849, the swim to dry ground alone): portal room 1/3, run 1 swam back from a block in the lake to the ground it had walked and went down (1296 s), run 2 timed out, run 3 died :no-pickaxe; stronghold 3/3. Batch stronghold-room-d (plan run 39138341075, with the cave floored): portal room 0/3, stronghold 3/3: run 1 swam back, staired and tunnelled to three over the frame 135 blocks off, then cut stairs after every tunnel that was on its way (tunnel-spent? counted steps, not ground gained), away from the frame, and walked back up them to the timeout; run 2 swam back, began its stairs, and after the first leg swam up again for dry ground (the shaft open to the sky), :stuck three times; run 3 over the mountain had its stairs :boxed three times under the ground. Now a tunnel is spent only when it came less than 4 nearer the frame, and the swim to dry ground is never chosen once the stairs or the tunnel have begun. Batch stronghold-room-e (plan run 39152932850): portal room 1/3, stronghold 3/3: run 2, the landing whose swim ended on a block in the lake (boxed in batches a, b and c), swam back to ground, staired and tunnelled to the frame in 1015 s; run 1 tunnelled under the lake to within a hundred blocks of the frame, fought mobs in the tunnel at Normal, died and came back with nothing, :no-pickaxe; run 3 over the mountain cut six legs of stairs to y 72 and had every stair and level step refused under the ground, :boxed three times in thirty seconds, as in batch d. Its recording replayed (probes 39158899900, 39159213076): the stairs were not under the ground but in the open air: the mountain's western slope falls faster than a staircase's one in one, so the sixth leg left it at y 83 into the sky over a flooded valley (water y 47 to 56, nothing solid for 48 blocks west and north at y 66), laid a floor every stair down to y 72, and there, fifteen over the water, every stair's floor was refused as a bridge over a fluid (stairs/over-fluid?, within 16) while each level step one block higher laid one more block of causeway, 32 east, until :boxed. Now, standing dry under the open sky with ground 4 or more lower toward the frame that a route reaches, the bot walks down to it (downhill), the stairs begin only where the surface stops falling. Batch stronghold-room2-a (plan run 39161847521): stronghold 3/3, portal room 1/3: run 3 walked the slope down from y 116 to 94 and staired from there through caves to y 33, where a lake lay sixteen under every stair's floor and the staircase crept level 32 east, laying a floor a step, and was :boxed three times, the shore 33 off (batch stronghold-room-a's run 3 had found its stair there on the 33rd step); run 2 by the lake died in the tunnel to mobs again, :no-pickaxe. Now a descent's level steps head for the nearest column where a stair's floor would stand (stairs/floor-distance) and have shore-reach more steps when one is in sight. Batch stronghold-room2-b (plan run 39178431697): portal room 3/3 (1172, 1034 and 613 s), stronghold 3/3: the mountain landing walked its slope down, staired through the caves, stepped to the lake's shore and tunnelled to the frame; both lake landings tunnelled under the lake to it. The stage's acceptance met: throw 5/5 (batch 265a), stronghold 3/3, portal room 3/3. In the post-pearls chain (batch chain-w5 run 1), a dry tunnel blocked by water near room height hit :no-way when within deep (8) over the frame; to-room now falls back to stairs down to room-over (1) over the frame."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/10-blazes-pearls-stronghold-end.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-end-and-dragon.md" "brain/bot/plan/stronghold.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :end-portal
  :problem/issue 266
  :problem/goals [:end-portal :enter-end]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. In the stronghold's portal room, with eyes of ender held, put an eye into each of the twelve frames that lacks one so the portal lights, then step into it and arrive in the End on the obsidian platform without walking off it into the void."
  :problem/needs
  ["Which frames lack an eye: the frame's state (end/eyed?), read from the loaded block, else the last sighting"
   "A cell the feet can stand in within reach of each frame that a route reaches: the frames float two blocks over the room's floor round a 3x3 pit of lava, so the far side of the ring is reached by walking on the frames themselves, 13/16 high, which a route must take for floors"
   "The way up to the frames from the room's floor: three stairs blocks with a silverfish spawner in the middle of the top step, so a route must climb stairs, a block at a time, up a side"
   "When the portal is lit: the server places the nine end portal blocks the moment the twelfth eye goes in (EndPortalFrameBlock.useItemOn); they are remembered like the frames"
   "When the End is reached: the respawn packet naming minecraft:the_end sets :player/dimension"
   "What takes the body into the portal: the end portal block has no collision, so feet over it drop into its cell, and the server moves the player at once (no four-second wait as at a nether portal)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A use-item while looking at a frame fills it: the throw trial looks up; here the look is at the frame on purpose, and a use-item-on on a frame that has its eye only acks"
   "Walking the ring: a misstep into the interior before the portal is lit is a fall of two into lava; the route refuses cells beside or over lava (path/clear?), and the frames are its only floors there"
   "A frame reached from under it, from the room's floor, is out of reach: the eye is 2.6 under the frame's top"
   "The ring on record is not whole: a frame's chunk unloaded or a frame unseen; the enter row waits :no-ring"
   "In the End the platform stands over the void: a route off its edge finds no landing and is refused, and the bot stands still once the row is done"
   "Endermen in the End and the dragon's first flight: nothing of this stage fights; the dragon is #267's"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["The work is a plan of ops read against the world each tick (build/work-op), as the nether portal's cast: the first frame without an eye is worked, so a death or a reload resumes where the world says, and nothing records progress"
   "The frames, the end portal and stairs are floors to a route (path/stood-on), since the physics' oracle already takes each for a full cube and the feet read their cell a half block up: a player walks the frames and climbs the stairs, and so does the bot"
   "The gym builds the vanilla portal room itself (gym/portal-room, StrongholdPieces.PortalRoom block for block, the frames facing inward as the game's own do) round a surface landing and lands the bot on the room's floor inside its door: locate structure names a stronghold's start, not its portal room, and no command finds the room; the real room is the stronghold stage's to reach (#265)"
   "The enter row's ops are the end portal row's and then a wait for the nine portal blocks and the step in: one plan builder with an enter? flag, as frame-plan takes one"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON: an end_portal block at the cell the bot remembers one (gym end-portal, :truth/at [:portal]); the bot in minecraft:the_end (gym enter-end, gym/dimension-test). sim_test: against the model's End, every frame eyed and nine portal cells placed; the dimension flips and the player stands on the platform."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never put an eye into a frame nor entered the End. steve's End attempts (f7 1/3/5) were slain by endermen before a single bed, with no kit server-side; ruststeve started its End gyms in the End by teleport and never crossed a portal. Batch end-portal-a (plan run 39132430055, c26ccd5): end-portal passed 3/3 (27 to 31 s from the room's floor to the lit portal), enter-end 3/3 (28 to 34 s to the End), the first eyes in frames and the first End of any clojurecraft bot; from the gym's own room, not a stronghold's: the way to a real room is #265's."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/10-blazes-pearls-stronghold-end.md"
